WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.268
-Thank you so much.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.804
And welcome, welcome, welcome,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:08.408
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's right!

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:10.376
Well, guys, today in Washington,

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:12.612
President Biden met virtually

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.981 line:0%
with Canadian Prime Minister
Justin Trudeau

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:17.149 line:0%
for the first time
since taking office.

00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:19.085 line:0%
Yeah, Biden did
the best he could

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.120 line:0%
to fix our relationship
with Canada.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.589
He was like, "Hey,
about the last four years...

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:26.359
[Canadian accent]
...sorry."

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.993
In response, Trudeau was like,

00:00:27.993 --> 00:00:30.630
"On behalf of Canada,
thank you for your friendship,

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.199
for your support,
and for taking Ted Cruz."

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:34.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.169
Yep, Trudeau and Biden
had a typical video chat

00:00:37.169 --> 00:00:39.672
between a 49-year-old
and a 78-year-old.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.341
Trudeau spent
the first 20 minutes

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.542
trying to tell Biden
he was on mute.

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:45.478
It's like --
"No. Stop yelling.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:48.882
God. Give me a pen.
'You're on mute.'"

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.649
But it was a productive meeting,

00:00:50.649 --> 00:00:53.086
other than when Biden started
talking about his second cousin

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:56.256
who once went over Niagara Falls
in a wooden barrel.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:01:01.461
"He survived, but he still hears
rushing water every time he...

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:03.162
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:05.498
...touches wood."

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:13.372
"He's now down
to only three nipples."

00:01:13.372 --> 00:01:14.807
Well, guys, this is exciting.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:17.276
The Golden Globes
are this Sunday, and --

00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:19.378
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:21.247
It was just announced

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.149
that some front-line
and essential workers

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:26.452 line:0%
have been invited
to attend this year's event.

00:01:26.452 --> 00:01:29.522 line:0%
That should be a fun red carpet
for the front-line workers.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.090
"Who am I wearing?

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:34.927
Dickies scrubs
and the same PPE since June.

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:36.595
That's who I'm wearing."

00:01:36.595 --> 00:01:38.531
They should be
a really good crowd.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.533
I mean, literally
the only people on Earth

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.902
who didn't spend the last year
binge-watching every movie

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.937
and show that came out.

00:01:44.937 --> 00:01:46.472
Some more TV news.

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:49.108
Last night was a new episode
of "The Bachelor,"

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:53.879
and for one of the dates,
Matt and Rachael went skydiving.

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:55.849
This is real.
Let's see how that went.

00:02:06.058 --> 00:02:09.862 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:12.732
-Yeah, yeah!

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.267
-Ohh!

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.871
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.806
-Wow.

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:22.008
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:24.076
Somehow we can land
a rover on Mars,

00:02:24.076 --> 00:02:28.614
but we can't land a "Bachelor"
contestant on Earth.

00:02:28.614 --> 00:02:32.185
Gosh. Alex, can we just see
just the end of that when she --

00:02:33.752 --> 00:02:36.222
[ Laughter ]
-Ohh!

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:39.792
-[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:42.194
When she asked the instructor,
"What gives, man?"

00:02:42.194 --> 00:02:45.131
He was like, "Wait. I thought
you were the instructor."

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:47.633
I think Rachael was still
a little out of it.

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:49.535
When Matt handed her a rose,
she said,

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:51.437
"Yes, I will answer this phone.

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:54.207
Yello? What's your problem?"

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:56.642
On the bright side,
Matt could finally use

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:57.910
that lame pickup line,

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:01.080
"Did it hurt when you fell
from heaven?

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.883
And smacked into the Earth?"

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.384
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:06.753
Yep, it was --

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:09.522
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:11.356
[ Rim shot ]

00:03:11.356 --> 00:03:13.259
It was hometowns week
on "The Bachelor" last night,

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.994
and things got pretty intense.

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:16.729
The emotions on that show
can be a little hard

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:19.032
to handle sometimes,
so I thought we could help.

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:21.934
Here's a clip from the episode
re-voiced

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:24.971
with the least emotional person
we know -- Siri.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:28.440
This is "Let's Get Siri-ous."

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.442
-Let's Get Siri-ous.

00:03:30.442 --> 00:03:33.145
-Siri: After talking
to my mom and Bri...

00:03:33.145 --> 00:03:36.282
♪♪

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:38.083
Ohh.

00:03:38.083 --> 00:03:42.955
So, like, I feel...

00:03:42.955 --> 00:03:44.557
like...

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:46.259
I'm falling in love with you.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:48.561
Thank you for sharing that
with me tonight.

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:52.432
[ Applause ]

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:54.033
-Some tech news.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.868
We're getting some details
about what Apple

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:58.003
might have planned
for the next iPhone,

00:03:58.003 --> 00:04:01.674
including portrait mode for
video, an ultra-wide camera,

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:05.711
and an attachable battery pack
so you can charge on the go.

00:04:05.711 --> 00:04:07.479
Right now,
Ted Cruz's wife is like,

00:04:07.479 --> 00:04:09.182
"Is there a feature
that tells you

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:12.151
which one of your group-chat
friends ratted you out?"

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:15.220
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:16.922
Well, this is interesting.

00:04:16.922 --> 00:04:18.691
The new iPhone is also rumored

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:21.994
to have a more grippy,
textured back.

00:04:21.994 --> 00:04:25.098
Aww. The iPhone is aging
just like the rest of us.

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:28.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:32.605
"Grippy, textured back."

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.973
Get this. Since the pandemic
has made it difficult

00:04:34.973 --> 00:04:36.575
for musicians to perform,

00:04:36.575 --> 00:04:40.646 line:0%
a German rock band has started
holding concerts in their van

00:04:40.646 --> 00:04:43.849 line:0%
for just one fan at a time.

00:04:43.849 --> 00:04:47.120 line:0%
Yeah, it's a German band
named "Das Awkward."

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:50.489
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.489 --> 00:04:52.524
That seems less like a concert

00:04:52.524 --> 00:04:55.394
and more like a hostage
situation, doesn't it?

00:04:55.394 --> 00:04:57.563
When they take requests,
the most popular one is,

00:04:57.563 --> 00:05:00.032
"Let Me Out."

00:05:00.032 --> 00:05:01.767
Well, this is big.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:04.503
I saw that New Jersey
just legalized marijuana.

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:07.307
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:12.945
And here now on the line
to discuss the historic moment

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:15.881
